---
/**
 * Layer 1 for the income tax calculator - sol-019's Answer.
 *
 * The page used to open on two columns of a computation and a badge, which
 * answers *what* and never *so what*. Design settled before the component in
 * `TaxAnswer.checks.md`.
 *
 * Three things it does that the columns could not:
 *   - headlines the MONTHLY bite, which is what a salaried person lives
 *     through, rather than the annual total (dd-010);
 *   - states the BREAK-EVEN, so the reader leaves with a rule they can apply
 *     next year without us (dd-003, dd-008);
 *   - renders every emphasis from one computed verdict, so the page can no
 *     longer recommend the losing regime (sol-043, dd-007/dont-2).
 *
 * Every id here is filled by the page's one script from one engine result.
 */
---

<section
  id="taxAnswer"
  class="rounded-2xl border border-navy-200 dark:border-white/10 bg-white dark:bg-navy-900/40 p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6"
  aria-label="Your income tax, answered"
>
  <p class="text-[10px] font-bold tracking-tight text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">
    FY 2025-26 · assessment year 2026-27
  </p>

  <!--
    The answer as a sentence, not a statistic. The value slots are fixed so the
    eye can return to them, and the prose around them stays true at every input
    (dd-008): it states what the figures ARE, never where the reader currently
    is.
  -->
  <div class="space-y-3">
    <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-navy-900 dark:text-white leading-snug">
      You&rsquo;ll pay
      <span id="ansMonthly" class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black tabular-nums">₹0</span>
      a month in income tax.
    </h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-300 leading-relaxed">
      That is <span id="ansAnnual" class="font-bold tabular-nums">₹0</span> for the year on
      income of <span id="ansGross" class="font-bold tabular-nums">₹0</span> — an effective
      rate of <span id="ansRate" class="font-bold tabular-nums">0%</span>. Spread evenly over
      twelve months; a real TDS schedule is not level, so treat the monthly figure as an
      average rather than a payslip line.
    </p>
    <p id="ansReconcile" class="text-sm text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400 leading-relaxed empty:hidden"></p>
  </div>

  <!--
    Both regimes, always, side by side. dd-006: the difference between them IS
    the lesson on this page, so it may never sit behind a switch. The winner's
    emphasis is applied by the script from `verdictFor()` - never by a class
    written here, which is the whole of sol-043.
  -->
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
    <div
      id="ansCardNew"
      class="rounded-xl border p-4 space-y-1 border-navy-200 dark:border-white/10"
    >
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
        <span class="text-[10px] font-bold tracking-tight text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">
          New regime
        </span>
        <span id="ansTagNew" class="text-[9px] font-bold tracking-tight px-2 py-0.5 rounded"></span>
      </div>
      <div id="ansTaxNew" class="text-2xl font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-white">₹0</div>
      <div id="ansSubNew" class="text-[11px] text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400"></div>
    </div>

    <div
      id="ansCardOld"
      class="rounded-xl border p-4 space-y-1 border-navy-200 dark:border-white/10"
    >
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
        <span class="text-[10px] font-bold tracking-tight text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">
          Old regime
        </span>
        <span id="ansTagOld" class="text-[9px] font-bold tracking-tight px-2 py-0.5 rounded"></span>
      </div>
      <div id="ansTaxOld" class="text-2xl font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-white">₹0</div>
      <div id="ansSubOld" class="text-[11px] text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!--
    The boundary, not the current position (dd-008/do-3). This is the idea the
    reader keeps: the new regime is a bet that their deductions fall short of a
    computable number.
  -->
  <p
    id="ansBreakEven"
    class="text-sm text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-200 border-t border-navy-200 dark:border-white/10 pt-4 leading-relaxed"
  >
  </p>
</section>
